  "details": "<p>According to La Trobe-Bateman and Niblett, this building was composed of\u00a0at least seven rooms. One of these had a pillared hypocaust and a geometric mosaic. To the west of the building was a 3m-wide road that led towards the temple precinct.\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Remains of a large building and baths uncovered between Bilbury Lane and Lower Borough Walls, beneath what is now known as the Gainsborough Spa in Aquae Sulis, modern-day Bath.",
